From 6eba867284e664da76aa3d28a5954fcb7ab6b6b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:31:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/45] Send sounds, entity visibility and civs in the Specula
 feed

Feed format v9. A sounds record before the turn record lists the sound
groups the turn played, in order: CCmpSoundManager's PlaySoundGroup,
PlaySoundGroupAtPosition and PlaySoundGroupForPlayer record them before
testing for a sound manager, which a nonvisual observer has none of. An
entity's sound carries its owner, position and visibility as of the
call, since it may be destroyed in the same turn.

Each turn entity gains the sound group of its current animation, which
CCmpVisualActor already resolves (ICmpVisual gets a C++-only getter),
and a mask of the players that see it, by the test PlaySoundGroup makes
for the displayed player. The players record gains each player's civ
and battle state, which the session GUI picks its music by.

Only reads are added, so the simulation and its hash are unchanged.
